  "body": "Follow-up of #3326 (PR #3997). Part of #1448.\n\n## What happens\n\nThe Face Geometry tab shows a Start point group and an Exit point group. The user types X and Y. The groups have no viewport Pick button.\n\nThe viewport pick of `crates/ui/src/start_exit_pick.rs` (`take`) writes to the 2D Contour only. The operation page disarms the pick when the open tab is not \"Lead in / Lead out\". The Face has its groups on the Geometry tab.\n\n## Expected\n\n- Each Face group has a Pick button, as the 2D Contour groups have.\n- A click on the part or the stock sets the pick in the draft. Apply commits it through `EditOperationParams`.\n- The pick snaps to a corner of the face region (`PickCapability::Raster`: \"Snaps to a corner\").\n\n## Done means\n\n- A UI test arms the Face start pick on the Geometry tab, gives a viewport pick, and reads the draft.\n- The same test for the exit pick.\n- The 2D Contour pick tests do not change.\n\n## Notes\n\nPR #3978 (Slot) changes `start_exit_pick.rs`. Do this work after that PR merges, or stack on it.\n",
